      "writtenOn": "2023-06-23T02:00:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the PE state is Ready.SNK, and that\u0027s meaningful, the TC should be in Attached.SNK, not AttachWait.SRC. I suspect that you\u0027re checking at not quite the right \"time,\" but something else could be going on.\n\nNit: Ideally, you would be testing something closer to the externally visible behavior of the port than the self-reported state of the state machine. The main externally visible requirement on the Sink during a Hard Reset is that it stop drawing current, but as I\u0027ve noted, there\u0027s no good way to test that in emulation currently.\n\nOne thing that\u0027s a little more tractable would be that the TCPM will have tried to switch the data and VCONN roles from their defaults during the initial connection, but they\u0027ll switch back during the reset, and the partner should be able to see that. This potentially suffers from the same timing issue as checking the internal state, in that you need to catch the TCPM at the right time or do something extra to keep it from swapping roles on its own. It would be unfair of me to ask you to try extra hard, though. The internal state checks are better than nothing.",
      "revId": "d1f16bd708f04fd41898238d5f2a3ae8757f02bb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
